(a) Investigation. The sheriff shall review the application for completeness and compliance with the terms of this article. The sheriff shall check if the charitable organization is registered with the secretary of state, or is exempt under O.C.G.A. § 43-17-9. The sheriff shall determine whether there are any records of complaints against the applicant or organizers in the records of the sheriff's department or the GCIC/NCIC crime database system. The sheriff may, at his/her/their discretion, conduct a background check of the organizers or corporate officers, or any other person named on the application. The sheriff may, at his/her/their discretion, make any other inquiries he/she/they deems necessary for the investigation of the applicant or the organizers.
